  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Differentiation in $\\mathbb{R}^n$ [S+N]\n\nFor $f : U \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^n \\to \\mathbb{R}^m$, \"differentiable at $x_0$\" means: there exists a **linear map** $L : \\mathbb{R}^n \\to \\mathbb{R}^m$ such that\n\n$$\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{\\|f(x_0 + h) - f(x_0) - L(h)\\|}{\\|h\\|} = 0.$$\n\nWhen such an $L$ exists, it's unique and called the **(total) derivative** $Df(x_0)$. Its matrix in standard coordinates is the **Jacobian**:\n\n$$Df(x_0) = J = \\begin{pmatrix} \\partial f_1 / \\partial x_1 & \\cdots & \\partial f_1 / \\partial x_n \\\\ \\vdots & & \\vdots \\\\ \\partial f_m / \\partial x_1 & \\cdots & \\partial f_m / \\partial x_n \\end{pmatrix}.$$\n\nThis notebook walks the standard hierarchy:\n\n1. Partial derivatives — the components of $J$.\n2. Total derivative as the *best linear approximation*.\n3. Critical pitfall: partials can exist without the function being differentiable.\n4. Chain rule in matrix form.\n5. Maxima symbolic Jacobians.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 57,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Partial derivatives\n\nFor $f : \\mathbb{R}^n \\to \\mathbb{R}$, $\\partial f/\\partial x_i$ is the ordinary 1D derivative obtained by treating all other variables as constants. Maxima's `diff()` does this directly.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f_scalar : x^2 * y + sin(x*y) + y^3$\nprint(\"f(x, y) =\")$\nf_scalar;\nprint(\"∂f/∂x =\")$\ndiff(f_scalar, x);\nprint(\"∂f/∂y =\")$\ndiff(f_scalar, y);",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 58,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "f(x, y) =\nsin(x*y)+y^3+x^2*y\n∂f/∂x =\ny*cos(x*y)+2*x*y\n∂f/∂y ="
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "x\\,\\cos \\left(x\\,y\\right)+3\\,y^2+x^2"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 58,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The Jacobian: stacking partials [S+N]\n\nFor $f : \\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^2$ given by $f(x, y) = (x^2 - y^2,\\; 2xy)$ (squaring as a complex map), Maxima can build the full Jacobian matrix.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f_components : [x^2 - y^2, 2*x*y]$\nstate_vars : [x, y]$\nJ : genmatrix(lambda([i, j], diff(f_components[i], state_vars[j])), 2, 2)$\nprint(\"Jacobian J =\")$\nJ;\nprint(\"det(J) at (1, 1) =\", determinant(subst([x=1, y=1], J)))$\nprint(\"(equals 4(x² + y²) = 8 here — so f is locally invertible)\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 59,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Jacobian J =\nmatrix([2*x,-(2*y)],[2*y,2*x])\ndet(J) at (1, 1) = 8\n(equals 4(x² + y²) = 8 here — so f is locally invertible)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The total derivative as best linear approximation\n\nGeometrically, $f(x_0 + h) \\approx f(x_0) + J(x_0)\\,h + o(\\|h\\|)$. The plane through $(x_0, f(x_0))$ tangent to the graph of $f$ has slope $J$.\n\nFor a scalar $f : \\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}$, this is the **tangent plane**:\n\n$$z = f(x_0, y_0) + f_x(x_0, y_0)(x - x_0) + f_y(x_0, y_0)(y - y_0).$$\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f_tan : x^2 + y^2$  /* paraboloid */\nfx : diff(f_tan, x)$\nfy : diff(f_tan, y)$\nx0 : 1.0$ y0 : 0.5$\nf_at : float(subst([x=x0, y=y0], f_tan))$\nfx_at : float(subst([x=x0, y=y0], fx))$\nfy_at : float(subst([x=x0, y=y0], fy))$\n\nprint(\"Tangent plane at (\", x0, \",\", y0, \"):\")$\nprint(\"  z =\", f_at, \"+\", fx_at, \"(x -\", x0, \") +\", fy_at, \"(y -\", y0, \")\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 60,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Tangent plane at ( 1.0 , 0.5 ):\n  z = 1.25 + 2.0 (x - 1.0 ) + 1.0 (y - 0.5 )"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Plot the surface and tangent plane.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "tangent_plane : f_at + fx_at * (x - x0) + fy_at * (y - y0)$\nax_draw3d(\n  explicit(x^2 + y^2, x, -2, 2, y, -2, 2),\n  title=\"z = x² + y² (paraboloid)\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"y\", zlabel=\"z\",\n  colorscale=\"Viridis\"\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
